Use io, list, and string.

Define function append_char taking target as a pointer to TcString, c as a byte:
    Append to target text (address of c) as a pointer to byte of length 1.
Done.

Let text be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr("PAYPALISHIRING"), bytes_len("PAYPALISHIRING")).
Let n be length of text.
Let row_count be 3.
Let rows be an empty list of text.
For every r from 0 to row_count - 1:
    Let blank be create an empty text.
    push blank to address of rows.

Let row start at 0.
Let direction start at 1.
For every i from 0 as an unsigned number to n - 1:
    Let cell be list_get(address of rows, row as an unsigned number).
    append_char(address of cell, text.data[i]).
    list_set(address of rows, row as an unsigned number, cell).
    If row is 0:
        Set direction to 1.
    If row is row_count - 1:
        Set direction to -1.
    Set row to row + direction.

Let answer be create an empty text.
For every r from 0 to row_count - 1:
    Let cell be list_get(address of rows, r as an unsigned number).
    Let cell length be length of address of cell.
    Append to address of answer text cell.data of length cell length.
Say answer.

For every r from 0 to row_count - 1:
    Let cell be list_get(address of rows, r as an unsigned number).
    str_free(address of cell).
str_free(address of answer).
list_free(address of rows).
str_free(address of text).
Return 0.
